# Read by `vite build`, which inlines these into the bundle — they are compile
# time values, not runtime ones, so changing them means rebuilding.
#
# Deliberately does not set VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#
# A production build resolves the API to the relative path `/api` (see
# src/config/env.ts), which the browser takes as the origin that served the
# page — and Caddy, which serves the bundle, proxies `/api` there to the
# backend. That makes the built bundle, and the image built from it, independent
# of the domain it is deployed to: the same tag runs on staging and production,
# and moving domains is an environment change rather than a rebuild.
#
# Naming a host here would undo that and pin every image built from this
# checkout to that one address. Set VITE_API_BASE_URL only for the arrangement
# the relative path cannot express — a backend on a different origin from the
# app — and expect the resulting bundle to be specific to it.

# Drives `isProduction` in config/env.ts, which hides the environment banner.
VITE_APP_ENV=production
